        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.groupme.com/v3/bots/post",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ bot_id: '75c281957bf9655f47833a5248', text: '⚠️ FB publish failed for ' + $('Loop Posts').item.json.scheduled_date + ' (attempt ' + (($('Loop Posts').item.json.publish_attempts || 0) + 1) + '/3): ' + (($json.error && ($json.error.message || JSON.stringify($json.error))) || 'unknown error') }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.3,
      "position": [2608, 432],
      "id": "wf4-groupme-fail-018",
      "name": "GroupMe Alert (failure)",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WF4 — runtime-config Page publisher (mirror of the live workflow)\n\nThis JSON is the repo MIRROR; the live WF4 (jpk9cLbvvvZxMMFi) is updated via MCP.\nKeep them in sync.\n\n**No FB credentials live here.** At runtime WF4:\n1. Fetches `fb_settings` (page id, graph version, `auto_publish_enabled`) and the\n   `fb_secrets.fb_page_access_token` from LP Supabase, authenticated by the n8n\n   credential **LP Supabase Account** (httpMultipleHeadersAuth: apikey + Authorization\n   headers). NOTE: $env.LP_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY did NOT work on this instance —\n   trigger runs failed; the credential store is the working pattern for all FB\n   workflow Supabase auth.\n2. **Gate:** publishes only when `auto_publish_enabled === true` AND page id + token\n   are present. OFF in /content/settings ⇒ instant no-op pause.\n3. **Query owns date + time + retry gates:** `status=approved & target in (page,both)\n   & page_posted_at is null & publish_attempts<3 & scheduled_date <= today(ET) &\n   (publish_at is null OR publish_at <= now)`. Future-dated posts wait for their\n   date; timed posts wait for their ET time (DB trigger derives publish_at).\n4. **Claim** PATCHes with `page_posted_at=is.null` + `Prefer: return=representation` —\n   if 0 rows come back another run already claimed it (idempotency).\n5. Publishes via `/photos` (image) or `/feed` (text); token in the BODY, never the URL.\n6. **Capture Post ID** normalizes the Graph response — downstream nodes must read\n   `$('Capture Post ID')`, never `$json`, or the comment id leaks into permalinks.\n7. **target='both' two-leg model:** always sets `page_posted_at`/`page_permalink`;\n   ONLY `target='page'` also flips `status='posted'`. A 'both' post stays 'approved'\n   until the human Group leg is recorded by `markPosted()` in the Dashboard.\n8. **Failure:** Graph error → `last_publish_error` + GroupMe alert; attempts increment\n   at claim, row drops out of the query at 3.\n\nNothing here posts to a Facebook GROUP (Meta deprecated that API in April 2024).",
        "height": 520, "width": 560
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [0, -480],
      "id": "wf4-note-0019",
      "name": "WF4 model"
    }
  ],
